For F_M = mg = 4905 N at g = 12.5 mm, the required current is

I = g\sqrt{\frac{mg}{K}}

The coil power is

P = I^2 R = \frac{mg}{K}g^2 R

For a typical EMS coil with K = 5 \times 10^{-4} N·m²/A² and R = 2 Ω, at g = 12.5 mm:

I = 0.0125\sqrt{\frac{4905}{5 \times 10^{-4}}} = 0.0125 \times 3132 \approx 39.2 \text{ A}

P = (39.2)^2 \times 2 \approx 3.1 \text{ kW}

For 7 actuators, the total hover power is approximately

P_{\rm total} \approx 7 \times 3.1 \approx 21.7 \text{ kW}

This exceeds the 20 kW limit. Reducing the gap to 10 mm gives P \approx 13.9 kW, within the limit. The gap range is therefore set to 10–15 mm, consistent with Transrapid's nominal gap of about 10 mm.

