Appendix H: Numerical Feasibility Study for the 10 m Demonstrator

H.1 Simulation Parameters

Parameter Value
Mass 500 kg
Wheelbase 1.5 m
Nominal gap 12.5 mm
Gap range 10–15 mm
Actuators 7 EMS + 1 LSM
Maximum force per EMS actuator 2000 N
Maximum LSM thrust 1500 N
Controller bandwidth 100 Hz
Simulation time step 0.1 ms

H.2 Disturbance Scenarios

1. Step disturbance:  d_z = 500  N applied at  t = 0.1  s.
2. Sinusoidal disturbance:  d_z = 300\sin(2\pi \times 5t)  N.
3. Gap measurement noise:  \sigma = 0.1  mm.
4. Actuator failure: One EMS actuator fails at  t = 0.5  s.

H.3 Fault Scenarios

1. Single actuator failure: Loss of one EMS actuator.
2. Power supply failure: Loss of all EMS actuators.
3. Sensor failure: Loss of gap sensor.
4. Controller failure: Loss of the primary controller.

H.4 Success Criteria

The demonstrator is considered successful if:

1. The gap remains within  [10, 15]  mm under all nominal disturbances.
2. The gap remains within  [8, 20]  mm under fault conditions.
3. Controlled landing is achieved within 2 s of fault detection.
4. Impact velocity is less than 1.5 m/s.
5. Maximum pitch and roll are less than 5° and 10°, respectively.
6. Power consumption is less than 20 kW.

H.5 Falsification Criteria

The architecture is falsified if:

1. The gap exceeds  [8, 20]  mm under any admissible fault.
2. Controlled landing is not achievable within 2 s.
3. Impact velocity exceeds 1.5 m/s.
4. The capture basin condition

\mathcal{K}_{\rm robust}^{\rm mag} \subseteq \operatorname{Capt}(K, \mathcal{C}_{\rm landing})

is violated for any state in the nominal operating envelope.



